  - family-names: "Bidisha"
    given-names: "Rubiya Tasfi"
    email: "rubiya.tasfi.bidisha@g.bracu.ac.bd"

repository-code: "https://github.com/niamul-anto/Fabric-Defect-Detection"

keywords:
  - fabric defect detection
  - fabric defect classification
  - deep learning
  - computer vision
  - object detection
  - image classification
  - FD-Net V2
  - lightweight neural network
  - PyTorch
  - YOLOv8
  - Faster R-CNN
  - RetinaNet
  - Vision Transformer
  - EfficientNet

abstract: >-
  This repository contains the implementation, evaluation scripts, benchmarking
  utilities, dataset-preparation tools, and experimental results for a deep
  learning-based fabric defect diagnosis framework. The research uses a
  self-developed and manually annotated four-class fabric defect dataset
  containing Cut, Hole, Stain, and ThreadError. The repository includes object
  detection experiments using YOLOv8m, RetinaNet, and Faster R-CNN, as well as
  image classification experiments using ViT-B/16, VGG16-BN,
  EfficientNet-B0, and the proposed scratch-trained lightweight FD-Net V2.
```
